ose would appear greyed out with a toast until the user syncs the full dataset, which seems like acceptable behavior.\n\nI'm now checking whether running the closure a second time (level 2) would pull in significantly more rows, which could push the dataset size up to around 10MB. I need to actually compute the level 2 and level 3 closure sizes to decide if that's worth doing.\n\n","startTime":1791953103752,"lastModifiedTime":1791953103752},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01HDbd5AFZ7nxBxDkQmy335A","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"cd /tmp/idiomdata && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nrows=[]\nfor i in range(1,6):\n    rows+=json.load(open(f'p{i}.json'))['data']\nbyw={r['word']:r for r in rows}; byid={r['id']:r for r in rows}\ndef compact(r): return {k:v for k,v in r.items() if v is not None}\ndef size(S): return len(json.dumps([compact(byid[i]) for i in S],ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':')).encode())\nS={r['id'] for r in rows if r.get('story') or r.get('opposite')}\nfor lvl in range(1,4):\n    N=set(S)\n    for i in S:\n        r=byid[i]\n        for w in (r.get('similar') or [])+(r.get('opposite') or []):\n            if w in byw: N.add(byw[w]['id'])\n    S=N; print(lvl,len(S),round(size(S)/1e6,2))\n    ex=sum(1 for i in S if byid[i].get('example')); src=sum(1 for i in S if byid[i].get('source')); print(' example',ex,'source',src)\n\"","description":"Compute closure sizes for seed subset","prefix_rule":"[\"python3\",\"-c\"]"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\n1 13863 8.42\n example 11340 source 13398\n2 14657 8.79\n example 11793 source 14169\n3 14816 8.86\n example 11880 source 14325\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/jm-spec71","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"auto","taskId":"d0wirt","output":"1 13863 8.42\n example 11340 source 13398\n2 14657 8.79\n example 11793 source 14169\n3 14816 8.86\n example 11880 source 14325\n","exitCode":0,"inBackgr